{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["And the reason for mentioning <b>You shall not round off the edge of your head</b> is like the practice of the nations, to be distinguished from them. And since the hair of the head and the beard were created for ornament, it is not fitting to destroy it. And some say that this verse is joined with 'nor shall you make a cut for a soul,' for there is one who destroys the edge of his head and also the edge of his beard on account of the dead."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:04.368952579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}